# Commentary.

**Authors:** Burgess, Robert L., Molenaar, Peter C. M.

## Abstract
Supports Gottlieb's conclusion that developmental behavior genetics is unsuitable for analyzing developmental coactional processes because it does not concern itself with mechanisms through which genotypes are transformed into phenotypes. But maintains that modern behavior genetics provides an indispensable tool to analyze nonlinear epigenetic processes. (MDM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ521900

